# App C Conventions

## Naming

- Functions / files: `snake_case` — `user_init`, `zc_uart_init`, `servo_open`
- Types / structs / enums / macros: `UPPER_SNAKE` — `GD_T`, `DEV_MANAGE`, `UART_FRAME_HEAD`, `SERVO_CMD_SET_ANGLE`
- Include guards: `_NAME_H` or `__NAME_H__` — `_UART_COMMUNICATION_H`
- Config switches: `TCFG_*`, `ENABLE`/`DISABLE`, `*_EN` in `app_config.h` / `app_modules.h`

## Logging

Always use the JieLi log pattern (do not invent another logger):

```c
#define LOG_TAG_CONST       NORM
#define LOG_TAG             "[module_name]"
#include "log.h"

log_info("...");
log_error("...");
```

Prefer `log_info` / `log_error` / `put_buf` over raw `printf` (except existing `DEV_DEBUG` stubs).

## Work model

- Drive work from the `get_msg` / `post_msg` loop in `toy_music_app()` (`MSG_4MS`, `MSG_24MS`, `MSG_300MS`, `MSG_UARTRX`, `MSG_UARTTX`, …)
- Keep UART/device ISRs thin; post messages instead of heavy work in IRQ
- Gate features with macros in `app_config.h` / `sh55/app_modules.h`, not ad-hoc `#if 0` sprawl

## Comments

Match nearby file style (Chinese protocol notes + English section banners are both common). Keep new public API comments clear and consistent with the file.
